{
  "schema": "lean-proof-simplification-evidence-v1",
  "source_commit": "224acccf569dd7126e02dc273ab9692bb423d5e6",
  "source_parent": "c91cc3f4caab6ec5b53ad5737bb1656e039f050f",
  "scope": "Simplify binary push division and remainder proofs and the two left-move bit bounds",
  "validation": "Paired target and all five tracked direct Lean clients compile. WangRowStep object matches; WangStrip, Occupation, RunTrace and PackingCells objects differ but their both-object-pinned namespace/type/axiom and global simp/instance probes match. Target declaration and registration probes match.",
  "limitations": [
    "The initial Occupation overlay failed from missing CellDecoding and was retried; baseline records combine first target/Strip successes and later client retries.",
    "CurrentKernelData2011 matches a prior input sample, not its producer; WangTable and MachineRun215 prior producer records have only one source digest. Other provider associations use prior source-matched producer receipts.",
    "Post-build path samples resolve older PellRecurrence, HalfBinomial, BinaryCarry and SignedPairs; these samples are not contemporaneous transitive load-time pins. Project, BusyBeaver, Foundation and Mathlib closure remains cached.",
    "Byte-different client objects have unestablished causes. Declaration/registration reports do not establish equality of proof bodies or every persistent extension. Single shared-load timing pairs are not general benchmarks.",
    "Compiled objects are excluded; recorded object hashes and provider paths require external objects for independent byte verification. The standalone arithmetic probe lacks full input pins."
  ],
  "archive": "inputs-and-logs.zip",
